          "text": "I now have the key control flow. Analyze:\n\n1. after on accepted success: In `_begin_iter`, if outcome exists and not explicit retry, `_run_retry` is added then `_post_retry_check_actions`. In `_post_retry_check_actions`, if not retry_run_result (i.e., accepted success — retry predicate returns False), it adds `lambda rs: rs.outcome.result()` and returns — `self.after` is only added when retrying. So `after` does NOT run on an accepted success. Value: false.\n\n2. wait computed before stop: In `_post_retry_check_actions` (when retrying), order: `self._add_action_func(self._run_wait)` then `self._add_action_func(self._run_stop)`. Actions run in list order in `iter`. So yes, wait duration computed before stop is evaluated. Value: true.\n\n3. before_sleep runs on the attempt where stop ends retries: In `_post_stop_check_actions`, if `stop_run_result` is true, it goes to retry_error_callback or exc_check, and returns — the `before_sleep` action (added after in next_action branch) is never reached. So no. Value: false.\n\n4. retry_error_callback replaces exhaustion error: yes — when stop result is true, if retry_error_callback, it's added as action and its return value becomes `do` returned by `iter`, which `__call__` returns. Value: true.\n\nCitations: use exact quotes from tenacity/__init__.py. Let me pick quotes carefully.\n\nFor claim 1:\n```\n    def _post_retry_check_actions(self, retry_state: \"RetryCallState\") -> None:\n        if not (self.iter_state.is_explicit_retry or self.iter_state.retry_run_result):\n            self._add_action_func(lambda rs: rs.outcome.result())\n            return\n\n        if self.after is not None:\n            self._add_action_func(self.after)\n```\n\nFor claim 2:\n```\n        self._add_action_func(self._run_wait)\n        self._add_action_func(self._run_stop)\n        self._add_action_func(self._post_stop_check_actions)\n```\nPlus iter loop:\n```\n        for action in self.iter_state.actions:\n            result = action(retry_state)\n```\n\nFor claim 3:\n```\n    def _post_stop_check_actions(self, retry_state: \"RetryCallState\") -> None:\n        if self.iter_state.stop_run_result:\n```\nand\n```\n        if self.before_sleep is not None:\n            self._add_action_func(self.before_sleep)\n```\nNote before_sleep is added only in the not-stopped branch, after next_action.\n\nFor claim 4:\n```\n            if self.retry_error_callback:\n                self._add_action_func(self.retry_error_callback)\n                return\n```\nAnd maybe `else: return do` from Retrying.__call__.\n\nAll quotes exact. Submit.",
